#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234975 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/id #uuid "4031c8a9-0559-5d8d-a1a5-6e3402c19b27" :question/math-academy-id "e-26133" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids ![](images/df/df720fc5b6471db8190154ad9e8c1a3094f3fe885f6150de21bb7a5ef0653be5.svg) and ![](images/ea/ea8dbe9b1e82824b527a7f87153b0ef9aa33e6af2f9f48ff5377b4ad19b48c2b.svg) whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n![](images/7c/7cf42f88ef110c2dea6d3ab150ed095c8845a4b3a110ae955e1c1da666bcc364.svg)\n\nFind ![](images/46/4694851f2a7762e81f5ff1328018557fee878a018c60f2b8db8be5b9775f24ee.svg) ![](images/65/65537e63a2f6c671139d4145c5157b89d95c0f6db5a0304d39f3aa0ee781a4a1.svg) and ![](images/ae/ae992fcbb9b6e797b7a06dda4dbedec893ebad102944c504a0de22790e75e940.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the ![](images/d4/d43a228fcfe8f3eeb60a2ce9ec2d0cca2ebd281c09cceef580587e8ef5672511.svg)-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n![](images/f9/f94b2d4acca3dae2e05ff1cc1ba860488de8ca4fd3b1468bf2f0287ac8fd208b.svg)\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the ![](images/d4/d43a228fcfe8f3eeb60a2ce9ec2d0cca2ebd281c09cceef580587e8ef5672511.svg)-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region:\n![](images/28/28f530c26d2a007471d7419a705b33a62378348c0bbfa9fab6f79e2aa0fa5fb2.svg)\nwhere ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) is the interior of the circle ![](images/1d/1d4b64030885f51b4f44e80010686c07bdb3e8d88386271543d08b91e6ad9d75.svg)\n\nAs a result, the volume of ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is given by\n![](images/00/0066a0d710b1f0a807ed0ece319744c6d826d0f7af56f8db4b88d8cb8ea3f652.svg)\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of ![](images/59/5914524b1d3db63c66998b75ca1d00a5dc4e294d2a8f10fe384d2b2ebf2af38e.svg) consists of\n\n- the lower part ![](images/68/687143de30f2e07f089e3e2d728d31db586a552ab6e9694dccb0612e0b6b6fa9.svg) and\n\n- the upper part ![](images/a1/a150d3381edb05cce1fdbbaf82b7364009114579fe1b0e647d004bff51b47d75.svg)\n\nfor ![](images/22/225fcd90b7a79b6f4559894a4ec6ffd00aa643ee0c83719e6ebd165764497f81.svg)\n\nTherefore, we have\n![](images/11/11b70e034ca321a0eeabaeac26e55564ef04951147a69d158a23795b4cd0d0c9.svg)\n\nSo,\n![](images/df/dfe19692ea883c7962ae2f7b539263c064afbab0012d5e9238f0046384de56b7.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129024 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "7dcea6be-fd16-5312-b50c-157bafcc2d65" :question/math-academy-id "e-8189" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR = \\Big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 1 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq z \\leq \\sqrt{2y}, \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq yz \\Big\\}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}{\\int }_{0}^{yz}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}[x]_{x=0}^{x=yz}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2y}}yz\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{2y}}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{y}{2}{(\\sqrt{2y})}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{y=1}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(8-1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129025 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/id #uuid "b0ad2f24-6f0c-5d66-9312-5e41840b4fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8190" :question/problem "![](images/04/043adf0ef683c24fbf4680145411d86fa94b52016bee44ac8f08ca7c5ca9f1b7.png)\n\n \n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the top one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/75/75a76a2dbc34c889335e66623e12b686eb9a255ee0d67f9be0e3792f2650360c.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type I region\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: (x,y) \\in D, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/e1/e19ffe6a0555851c2b05526272beb21dbcdc082a23a2e11809c661666efdf133.png)\n\nHence, the type I representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR = \\big\\{ (x,y,z) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 1, \\:\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 2, \\:\\: 0 \\leq z \\leq 4-x-y \\big\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-x-y}dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[z]_{z=0}^{z=4-x-y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(4-x-y)-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x-y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(4-x)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}((4-x)(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6-2x\\,dx \\\\  & =[6x-{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =(6(1)-{1}^{2})-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129026 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/id #uuid "7883263b-110b-558f-83b2-0f6ec28be2c5" :question/math-academy-id "e-8191" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surface ![](images/9c/9c7c9aac6c94031d8430a8e8a2e4d3678a640379cdbc173fc5209ea532f3191b.svg) the plane ![](images/6c/6c78648d93eec934cde0f90387e06783c3d777a7a445e39afc2e5fa91bc2ec0c.svg) and the planes ![](images/89/89c97ad93c125fc2b6f61d44fe9a90845fd289329d79d506c857f970d7586540.svg) ![](images/36/36fdd3a0fb618d9692c52fd9bcb6e916441dee88dbce405fb885ec0f7782f047.svg) ![](images/6b/6be447d259b9b63c2cdd7adc4107d7c96ed4df1730890fc1bb5ce7cd585b8ea6.svg) ![](images/e0/e0f55ae8b32c4b9d5e58808c159b7433fd6e5b9db2212ecdf719869ea230a010.svg)" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type III region.\n\nFor each point ![](images/49/494198ee647d85e4442556a23f0c2d56aa601367360c321385ffc94523c47d73.svg) in the rectangular base region\n![](images/2d/2d0c4af57f0ba5e29300533e6ab0d95ce702b9d75bf175cbb9ffdca5f371d634.svg)\nthe variable ![](images/1d/1d9b846cface9f9348e4081a0dd87dd254bf26663c12aa0d1a15aa24d2393261.svg) runs from the surface\n![](images/72/72a6a2c2ba533fff74fe6ff80bafa9db62c3cbbc81f8be01cb7f5846b95f8dc8.svg)\nup to the plane\n![](images/36/3692729086c0564b65a7865e92dc2d5930f72b59abc0ea7634cd6dfa539b71b1.svg)\n\nSo we can write:\n![](images/d7/d7f58e8932311896757dffef5a240cb53a2b5e0b439455dbf83be832c8c15a01.svg)\n\nTherefore, the volume of ![](images/08/085f4d77675f3cb7323d94feaa9eaa38f2fecb26c0f8483895f9ddf36b8d319d.svg) is given by the following triple integral:\n\n![](images/1e/1e0c7ab5158a2e2dab67f2efae6ef29ac6be9e38bb9613c9c00a96d24c377a93.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412201 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec6ec01-733e-5f02-af23-9cc8caaac3a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412118} {:answer/id #uuid "7908b9c9-85f1-5fb7-8993-c1b1c1be6014" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412124} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a79b99-32b0-5d67-90f5-be49d7031cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412146} {:answer/id #uuid "bc206240-eb24-501d-9e9e-fc7fd50a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412147} {:answer/id #uuid "d8ffd103-8f74-5398-842a-0cf2cb86197a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bc206240-eb24-501d-9e9e-fc7fd50a7902" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412147} :answer-field/id #uuid "3acdc6ec-2a12-547a-88f2-73cc8411f0a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89162549-49ec-507f-b56c-dea9e66a6c30" :question/math-academy-id "q-161654" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1-x\\le y\\le 1+x,\\,0\\le z\\le xy}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}[z]_{z=0}^{z=xy}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{1-x}^{1+x}xy\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=1-x}^{y=1+x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+x)^{2}-(1-x)^{2})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}((1+2x+{x}^{2})-(1-2x+{x}^{2}))\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}(4x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412205 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f453de-fdf1-55b9-a976-f40753f1a395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412087} {:answer/id #uuid "2b56129c-0df0-54af-906e-0e2a10719caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412090} {:answer/id #uuid "6a682a9c-2f58-50f5-aa7f-1f1a6a470892" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412116} {:answer/id #uuid "b002bf51-05e0-5a47-b8cd-c23d9bd55718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412143} {:answer/id #uuid "d0dfa491-fc3b-502e-9e30-73d701d08848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b56129c-0df0-54af-906e-0e2a10719caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412090} :answer-field/id #uuid "03f2be2d-3077-50fe-b425-7498945d27f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aad5f44f-02bf-597c-9fc6-961b47dea0e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161655" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,1\\le z\\le 12-2x-2y}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type I region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{1}^{12-2x-2y}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[z]_{z=1}^{z=12-2x-2y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}12-2x-2y-1\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{4}11-2x-2y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[11y-2xy-{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}44-8x-16\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}-8x+28\\,dx \\\\  & ={[-4{x}^{2}+28x]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =-4+28-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f0d55a-8633-510a-9a70-0736d72c9ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412078} {:answer/id #uuid "140ba5b3-f14b-5987-a9e4-2138a251c985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412081} {:answer/id #uuid "34344a8f-e42d-5906-a0f4-0118a32ca456" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412096} {:answer/id #uuid "4b93a894-d471-5a0c-8e36-7dddcddd6b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412105} {:answer/id #uuid "75aa6ac2-cabd-5bdd-acc2-9cb3ddfbe7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412120}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b93a894-d471-5a0c-8e36-7dddcddd6b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412105} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ecbee3-5932-5b02-a688-7cc7061ce624" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "341b5b80-395a-52ac-87f9-9ef65cfdd0e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161658" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le y,\\,0\\le x\\le 3-y-z}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type II region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{3-y-z}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}[x]_{x=0}^{x=3-y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}3-y-z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(3-y)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3-y)y-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}-0 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d6a5b58-75ec-53ab-a1d2-eb0bf32cf642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412092} {:answer/id #uuid "77a79373-1a09-54a3-a0eb-c907112d07e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412122} {:answer/id #uuid "9abd54bf-c0ef-5909-85ca-4e4eaf1cbed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{33}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412134} {:answer/id #uuid "b1cec824-ea51-56e4-b35a-71eecbf948d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412144} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6589a0-a2f1-5e12-abad-5d645468e2ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d6a5b58-75ec-53ab-a1d2-eb0bf32cf642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412092} :answer-field/id #uuid "e818f6e1-d129-5503-b9af-07473e5656ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9b5b7d1e-4726-5549-b494-2d265b26d8f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-161661" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 4,\\,4\\le z\\le 8-x,\\,0\\le y\\le 2-\\frac{x}{2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}{\\int }_{0}^{2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}[y]_{y=0}^{y=2-\\frac{x}{2}}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{4}^{8-x}2-\\frac{x}{2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2}){[z]}_{z=4}^{z=8-x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(8-x-4)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}(2-\\frac{x}{2})(4-x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}8-4x+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[8x-2{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=4} \\\\  & =(8(4)-2(4)^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}(4)^{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412204 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e734a5-9af1-5a3f-a46d-a162b5a9d695" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{e+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412100} {:answer/id #uuid "51305570-7e81-503d-b280-1a6b6c9987cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2e-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412106} {:answer/id #uuid "7689dc2f-af85-5ca5-a2a8-2139c0233923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(e-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412121} {:answer/id #uuid "7d20b026-3d9d-51c7-8175-5393375b389e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412125} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d5f2f2-e19c-5d2f-b13d-328077613c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({e}^{2}+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412163}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7689dc2f-af85-5ca5-a2a8-2139c0233923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(e-1)^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412121} :answer-field/id #uuid "800556b7-3ddd-58c6-9180-e4db5ee1fa57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a3e6ac6a-7505-5f3b-b93d-b1ca31a35457" :question/math-academy-id "q-161678" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane, the surface $z={e}^{x+y},$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=1,$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {e}^{x+y}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{x+y}}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z={e}^{x+y}}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{x+y}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+1}-{e}^{x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[{e}^{x+1}-{e}^{x}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =({e}^{1+1}-{e}^{1})-({e}^{0+1}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}-e-e+1 \\\\  & =(e-1)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21737989-20b9-57bc-85fb-dd005e7013e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412086} {:answer/id #uuid "57a63e65-0af5-535e-921f-cf26a087a94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412110} {:answer/id #uuid "5f30f736-8249-5434-939a-dfd31765c473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412112} {:answer/id #uuid "cf5445c4-6f49-583f-8849-0c5d5fb4458f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412155} {:answer/id #uuid "d89e5e2c-05a3-56e2-a145-80c8cf2036a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21737989-20b9-57bc-85fb-dd005e7013e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412086} :answer-field/id #uuid "f31a7306-1b8a-5b78-bf95-372025264fa5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412192}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ddd03f9-52bb-5aac-ab6f-e8e23245dd8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161679" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane and the plane $z=x+y+2,$ and the planes $x=-1,$ $x=0,$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le x+y+2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x+y+2}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=x+y+2}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x+y+2\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{[(x+2)y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+2+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x+\\frac{5}{2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}x]}_{x=-1}^{x=0} \\\\  & =0-(\\frac{1}{2}(-1)^{2}+\\frac{5}{2}(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{5}{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412193 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c00395f-9e82-5707-bf92-e864ad8edc0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412091} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4f7933-2872-53eb-b6fc-0e473411ef59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412103} {:answer/id #uuid "4b7b318d-9356-52d1-916e-d034ec92dd98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412104} {:answer/id #uuid "553eead2-a9e1-5860-9f23-0d10dc994fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412109} {:answer/id #uuid "ce289eef-aceb-5a72-b3dc-c74255c1aae6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "553eead2-a9e1-5860-9f23-0d10dc994fc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412109} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aa2decc-c0b9-5e4c-ba07-85849fb1c3ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "248b6467-c247-56b8-869d-ac65691d4383" :question/math-academy-id "q-161682" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the surfaces $x=-{z}^{2}$ and $x=\\sqrt{y},$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=1,$ $z=-1,$ $z=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,-1\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,-{z}^{2}\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}{\\int }_{-{z}^{2}}^{\\sqrt{y}}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}[x]_{x=-{z}^{2}}^{x=\\sqrt{y}}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{y}-(-{z}^{2})\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\sqrt{y}+{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[z\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{3}{z}^{3}]}_{z=-1}^{z=2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2-(-1))\\sqrt{y}+\\frac{1}{3}({2}^{3}-(-1)^{3})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3\\sqrt{y}+3\\,dy \\\\  & ={[2\\sqrt{{y}^{3}}+3y]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}+3(1)-0 \\\\  & =2+3 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c05b87c-0a2f-5b02-9732-195c4cebeb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412084} {:answer/id #uuid "3efc03d6-4a00-528f-9d96-c985b96a5a27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412099} {:answer/id #uuid "52c8cce2-caca-5867-98e7-2a89cae75f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412107} {:answer/id #uuid "d74a887e-50b3-566c-a5b5-055f90be3eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412158} {:answer/id #uuid "ee22bbbb-c1bb-5206-b091-b3f1ee42854b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c05b87c-0a2f-5b02-9732-195c4cebeb2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412084} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f278fd-49bc-544f-84b1-fa3bfe926285" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d44ebfc0-d493-5ede-9c33-adfa1ab81dd9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161691" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0645201b3726750226811e0c714dc09d3075021fcbb6ddd1525748e9539c02d.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/c4/c4cf12ec9b53282620c1730f824c96d98e0b9dbabee0478bf258cf6c2741da81.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b497e6ef73b5b16e11baa08819e9628d3b5e1f2ee4d05fbafec48f73e087cbf1.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 1+y+z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1+y+z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=0}^{x=1+y+z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+y+z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}1+y+z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(1+y)z+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}1+y+\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}+y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{1}{2})-0 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a27f60c-16b5-569b-abbc-aa4449466aca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412115} {:answer/id #uuid "78c385a2-5f4c-581a-a6f9-b4926008f5e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412123} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff26051-514e-5c18-bb7b-c4d7ef1b02ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412126} {:answer/id #uuid "a12ab945-9736-5c00-9653-22301a0134af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412135} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf66a35-0d60-5e2a-ad38-2633147f2e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412171}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdf66a35-0d60-5e2a-ad38-2633147f2e6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412171} :answer-field/id #uuid "75d99bbb-fb44-5da4-9aad-fb7e625498f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4ef656bf-166c-5181-a3cb-7a7a57c705a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-161692" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7fe261b981f8c97a123675d1385237d62cdbb8c9976dc8c3f1841f073e497de.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/ca/ca8ce5a3ed7f3f164b348268cd0805e05df1e0ad8bf3381ca6368421ffe380cc.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-y+2z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/52/52f67235db14b903955660728642ed6b00603a12f480501767a98058f47d157a.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-y+2z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y+2z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y+2z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-y+2z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2-y+2z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(2-y)z+{z}^{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((2-y)(3)+{3}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}15-3y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[15y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =(30-6)-0 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0846e1fd-4ddb-5928-9bfb-cd2dba987965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412076} {:answer/id #uuid "2b03de32-d32b-50f3-9d81-a9356d8226fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412089} {:answer/id #uuid "80809090-d5dd-5ad5-8948-4e33b67f495a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412127} {:answer/id #uuid "84e5b082-ea93-5227-8dcc-35b31f9f13c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412130} {:answer/id #uuid "d45c8daf-95fb-55e5-89c7-d36d75897c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d45c8daf-95fb-55e5-89c7-d36d75897c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412157} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b3b1258-5fda-5712-badd-881fc05d24bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6e182344-0946-5483-a450-ce9ff2b36770" :question/math-academy-id "q-161693" :question/problem "![](images/4f/4f1ccfc3bdde9872114cc10c333f4d5dfcb1a271e97a3e37a58eefcb7eff1a48.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/a9/a90ab6eea35b1290e49106ac96c98241f637173c079812048feea9b25d911971.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/b4/b497e6ef73b5b16e11baa08819e9628d3b5e1f2ee4d05fbafec48f73e087cbf1.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2+2y-z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2+2y-z}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2+2y-z}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2+2y-z)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2y-z\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[(2+2y)z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2+2y-\\frac{1}{2}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{2}+2y\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}y+{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}+1)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412207 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ab8e05-2f75-5f1a-81dd-e07557bc4267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412075} {:answer/id #uuid "18508c80-0e18-52e8-aaa1-c7e154a4a945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412083} {:answer/id #uuid "1c0c0737-e66b-54ce-a699-eb6eaa91aed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412085} {:answer/id #uuid "33546658-bf3e-5faf-af2d-8c9d52241a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412095} {:answer/id #uuid "adf7bc54-9182-550e-91a1-e85a8bb8a42a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ab8e05-2f75-5f1a-81dd-e07557bc4267" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412075} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f638fd3-87cf-5489-b15f-bb90365aa5c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412186}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bc1d5c0b-7b74-5ad3-bb28-1b0236b6db17" :question/math-academy-id "q-161698" :question/problem "![](images/59/599b5392add89a6a22eb6c2232fedbdd26704ebf849bb05d7de52a6d81dcfb6a.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the right one, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/59/599b5392add89a6a22eb6c2232fedbdd26704ebf849bb05d7de52a6d81dcfb6a.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type III region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{2}-z},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2}\n$$\n\nis the projection of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/9e/9e7c6fad45d9d85bad5ca16a2000e4d44a1739ab70797e41ae94945a4ffb02ef.png)\n\nHence, the type III representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3-\\frac{x}{2}-z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3-x/2-z}dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[y]_{y=0}^{y=3-x/2-z}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(3-\\frac{x}{2}-z)-0\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}3-\\frac{x}{2}-z\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[(3-\\frac{x}{2})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}]}_{z=0}^{z=2}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}((3-\\frac{x}{2})(2)-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})-0\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}4-x\\,dx \\\\  & ={[4x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(8-2)-0 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412196 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0186ed58-f7ec-5ef6-80f2-6bba068af8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412073} {:answer/id #uuid "be2a6615-1145-511b-9323-6d645e89147a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412148} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f805af-86dc-564f-858f-cced5da9ea34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412152} {:answer/id #uuid "f263eb51-d454-599d-b9cd-c5c5f0283652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8+6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412166} {:answer/id #uuid "fa0bab28-2df9-528c-9c6b-acadde9b6b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+6{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7f805af-86dc-564f-858f-cced5da9ea34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412152} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8f622f-5689-5e59-b05c-8fbe8f53d165" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412189}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3fb0f5ed-20e1-5a6f-bec1-d9ddd1ad73da" :question/math-academy-id "q-161703" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $z=4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=2.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}^{4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-(2+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le x\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}}}\\,2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(2-2{x}^{2})+(2-2{x}^{2})+(2-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =6-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412208 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1407e0b5-2eac-5dcf-97da-330b75efe172" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412080} {:answer/id #uuid "712fd8f9-843f-5c8f-83e7-586d651bb279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412119} {:answer/id #uuid "aaa3893e-c007-5ed9-922a-6ed000a03c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412137} {:answer/id #uuid "cc47797d-8b5a-58ec-a3c6-0ec302e19804" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-3{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412153} {:answer/id #uuid "f95fe073-7d62-58ea-99d1-5ed1da13c971" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27+27{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaa3893e-c007-5ed9-922a-6ed000a03c46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412137} :answer-field/id #uuid "25ccf850-549b-5aa0-8084-8546dd642420" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d28d127a-2ef1-5397-a112-fbe0142a6964" :question/math-academy-id "q-161717" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y=-4+{x}^{2}$ and $y=5-{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4+{x}^{2} & =5-{z}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,-4+{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 5-{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-4+{x}^{2}}^{5-{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(5-{z}^{2})-(-4+{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-3\\le x\\le 3.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-3}^{3}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}}}\\,9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{9-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(9-{x}^{2})+(9-{x}^{2})+(9-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =27-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412194 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129206 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43198aae-a4dd-5b79-803a-1bb625a96355" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "553cda93-dcb2-5e16-b4c0-6ae818e9e098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412108} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8412c6-b5ae-5e4e-8894-ef77a1531b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412131} {:answer/id #uuid "9081743f-8252-523c-aefd-cf033c9164c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412132} {:answer/id #uuid "9680b5da-cca4-55bb-9bba-6bb3fc907b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412133} {:answer/id #uuid "bffefc4b-533b-5a59-a2a7-3d67fb1ca1ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "553cda93-dcb2-5e16-b4c0-6ae818e9e098" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412108} :answer-field/id #uuid "133b7b39-61d0-5df1-8fb5-ebbf0005ae7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c5e175a-7b49-566c-a1ad-cebab486783a" :question/math-academy-id "q-161741" :question/problem "![](images/da/daedf62c68ba62dee844cf17efc2d767da47a06ceccaedde854779f542b90114.png)\n\nFind the volume of the solid region above.\n\n*Hint: All surfaces, except for the front and right ones, are parallel to the corresponding coordinate planes.*" :question/worked-solution "![](images/7c/7c1738e97bc16a32f86d6901136afc4d9e288035d170fcd640db340ad36d19c5.png)\n\n \n\nNotice that our solid can be written as the type II region\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the projection of $R$ onto the $yz$-plane.\n\nTo find the top boundary curve of $D$ in the form $z=z(y),$ we substitute $x=1$ into the equation $x=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z:$\n\n$$\n1=2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z\\,⟹\\,z=2-\\frac{2}{3}y\n$$\n\nThen, we have\n\n$$\nD={(y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/ea/ea8b8397163309a11aa478fcc21ab53ee293c19f0d77a93b5c3d3472bb0eba70.png)\n\nHence, the type II representation of $R$ is\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 3,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 2-\\frac{2}{3}y,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 2-\\frac{1}{3}y-\\frac{1}{2}z}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-y/3-z/2}dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}[x]_{x=0}^{x=2-y/3-z/2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}(2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2})-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2-2y/3}2-\\frac{y}{3}-\\frac{z}{2}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[(2-\\frac{y}{3})z-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}]}_{z=0}^{z=2-2y/3}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}((2-\\frac{y}{3})(2-\\frac{2y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}{(2-\\frac{2y}{3})}^{2})-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})((2-\\frac{y}{3})-\\frac{1}{4}(2-\\frac{2y}{3}))\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(2-\\frac{2y}{3})(\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{y}{6})\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}3-\\frac{4y}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\,dy \\\\  & ={[3y-\\frac{2{y}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{27}]}_{y=0}^{y=3} \\\\  & =(3(3)-\\frac{2(3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{3}^{3}}{27})-0 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "019b4327-5ad2-57c4-991f-ae345072327b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}+\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412074} {:answer/id #uuid "834a8547-3c7e-58d8-acbd-c93cf9168259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412129} {:answer/id #uuid "af2f71bd-644d-5868-b8fa-2f4b088b1569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412140} {:answer/id #uuid "afcf7783-64e2-56a0-8cfb-04b04bdbf5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412142} {:answer/id #uuid "e14ce939-3279-5852-835b-269ab0e44698" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}-\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afcf7783-64e2-56a0-8cfb-04b04bdbf5d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412142} :answer-field/id #uuid "6365448d-1520-532c-a959-d9aa6da7c99c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412183}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d60206f-2159-50c2-97e6-e576ed41d216" :question/math-academy-id "q-38895" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $xy$-plane, the surface $z=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ and the planes $x=0,$ $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ $y=0,$ $y=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,dz\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[z]_{z=0}^{z=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-0\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x(\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{x=0}^{x=\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412198 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a53e873-260c-523d-86d2-7a180a1002fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412088} {:answer/id #uuid "419aa363-49d4-5a7e-8648-41b4d89d3360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412101} {:answer/id #uuid "5a35c9bc-b0cc-547d-b618-465e5dc40b31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12-6{x}^{2}-6{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412111} {:answer/id #uuid "c5d89b6f-0e3c-592b-8ec6-ea236b410b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-8{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412150} {:answer/id #uuid "f1627d2e-6e9b-5b03-86e7-80be1ddf0ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "419aa363-49d4-5a7e-8648-41b4d89d3360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412101} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea386800-ecda-5f25-a01e-e6b7ef7365e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59448eff-6a38-5971-9e73-20a5809538bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-38899" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $z=-7+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}$ and $z=1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,y)\\,dy\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xy$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & =1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xy$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type I region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,y)\\in D,\\,\\,-7+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}\\le z\\le 1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=8.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{-7+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}}^{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-(-7+3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}8-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $y=-\\sqrt{8-2{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $y=\\sqrt{8-2{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-2\\le x\\le 2.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}8-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{8-2{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{8-2{x}^{2}}}\\,8-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,dy\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{8-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{8-2{x}^{2}})}^{2}+(8-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =(8-2{x}^{2})+(8-2{x}^{2})+(8-2{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =24-6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129205 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb891682-26ae-541c-a92d-a79756d1714e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34c83166-7494-5134-b177-dcd7f8751b56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412097} {:answer/id #uuid "6594fd8f-7b74-5439-ac33-7bfcb0497e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412113} {:answer/id #uuid "81bffb26-ac25-55bf-8e70-fc8fa0c1f3e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412128} {:answer/id #uuid "ab25cad1-cd37-5991-b571-041028cd4125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412138} {:answer/id #uuid "af4d0a8b-1782-5c16-9feb-e54dff10e54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "af4d0a8b-1782-5c16-9feb-e54dff10e54a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412141} :answer-field/id #uuid "4313eb1e-43e2-5591-a760-a6cd81db0c05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e95b54dd-6268-5c5c-a490-a7470ea8eb6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-40305" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid $R,$ given by\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,-1\\le z\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that we have a three-dimensional type III region.\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2}\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[y]_{y=1}^{y={x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2}\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+2)-1\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}+1\\,dz\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[({x}^{2}+1)z+\\frac{2{z}^{3}}{3}]}_{z=-1}^{z=1}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}+1)(1-(-1))+\\frac{2}{3}({1}^{3}-(-1)^{3})\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}+\\frac{10}{3}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3}+\\frac{10}{3}x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{2}{3}(2)^{3}+\\frac{10}{3}(2))-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412206 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f5010d-f686-51ba-a29d-c3e7ebee57db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412077} {:answer/id #uuid "15b92e61-6c44-5617-9e76-b9e56e391b4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18+5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412082} {:answer/id #uuid "30e725ff-8723-507a-9752-9f42c6ef01be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18-18{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412093} {:answer/id #uuid "326b02ee-8bcd-58c7-ab55-05f61874238e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9+5{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412094} {:answer/id #uuid "695a6dc7-cbc3-59a8-b915-157fba409c04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25-25{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08f5010d-f686-51ba-a29d-c3e7ebee57db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412077} :answer-field/id #uuid "067e6f74-92ec-5ad2-b12e-786bdf4c3f9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b5335202-1eb7-59f8-9c44-3e9c073e7a32" :question/math-academy-id "q-40319" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the paraboloids $x=5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ and the parabolic cylinder $x=9-4{y}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{a(y)}^{b(y)}\\,f(y,z)\\,dz\\,dy\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $yz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9-4{y}^{2} \\\\ 9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $yz$-plane is an ellipse.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(y,z)\\in D,\\,\\,5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}\\le x\\le 9-4{y}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the ellipse $9{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=9.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}^{9-4{y}^{2}}\\text{d}x]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(9-4{y}^{2})-(5{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-1\\le y\\le 1.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}}}\\,9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dy.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f & ={(-\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{9-9{y}^{2}})}^{2}+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2})+(9-9{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =27-27{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186412203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235284 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13f9ed67-24d8-5d41-8f82-1296abc57f12" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Double-Integral Formula for Volume"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a84a3b2-19bb-5e84-a08f-3c6a06d39e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48+48{x}^{2}+{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412079} {:answer/id #uuid "4266d086-c362-56bc-8103-56ba8b41b6ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412102} {:answer/id #uuid "aa6f6ceb-2943-5ebc-887b-3670e50c46fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412136} {:answer/id #uuid "c61ccb94-219f-5803-be81-a5fe57c3ab73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412151} {:answer/id #uuid "fd66624b-ebb2-5780-9891-34dd31114da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa6f6ceb-2943-5ebc-887b-3670e50c46fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412136} :answer-field/id #uuid "130fe27f-0430-583d-a4a3-c1d6d680d596" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a2dc848f-1abc-53f8-b5eb-d94beb1dc593" :question/math-academy-id "q-40359" :question/problem "Consider the solid enclosed between the parabolic cylinders $y={x}^{2}$ and $y=16-{z}^{2},$ whose volume can be written in terms of double integrals, as follows:\n\n$$\nV={\\int }_{-4}^{4}{\\int }_{a(x)}^{b(x)}\\,f(x,z)\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nWhat is ${a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to determine the projection of the intersection of our surfaces onto the $xz$-plane. So, let's find where they intersect.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =16-{z}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the projection of the intersection in the $xz$-plane is a circle.\n\nNotice that our solid can be written as a type III region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,(x,z)\\in D,\\,\\,{x}^{2}\\le y\\le 16-{z}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is the interior of the circle ${x}^{2}+{z}^{2}=16.$ \n\nAs a result, the volume of $R$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}[{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{16-{z}^{2}}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(16-{z}^{2})-({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}16-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the boundary of $D$ consists of \n\n- the lower part $z=-\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}},$ and\n\n- the upper part $z=\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}},$\n\nfor $-4\\le x\\le 4.$ \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}16-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-4}^{4}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}^{\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}}}\\,16-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}\\,dz\\,dx.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}+{b}^{2}+f(y,z) & ={(-\\sqrt{16-{x}^{2}})}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{16-{z}^{2}})}^{2}+(16-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =(16-{x}^{2})+(16-{x}^{2})+(16-{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}) \\\\  & =48-3{x}^{2}-{z}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129766 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129207 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2c89813f-95aa-50b9-9bab-eec718bd34cd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Solid Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aa5673c-b507-5eb0-b945-e8326bea0f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{81}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412098} {:answer/id #uuid "6e45224d-66f6-5baf-b658-0f0390c00d1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412117} {:answer/id #uuid "b950298e-588d-50e8-91e2-a245f827cbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412145} {:answer/id #uuid "e74dcd89-af2d-524e-810b-cae923b4eb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{93}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412162} {:answer/id #uuid "f4c2ff78-cfe5-5246-b9cd-7e49b93095ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b950298e-588d-50e8-91e2-a245f827cbf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412145} :answer-field/id #uuid "27c4624f-447a-5116-b81e-664c77c5bd9e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186412178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0fac0ad3-f7f8-517d-a7fd-3686f90064e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-40396" :question/problem "Find the volume of the solid region enclosed by the $yz$-plane, the surface $x=6yz+12,$ and the planes $y=0,$ $y=2,$ $z=0,$ $z=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that our solid can be written as a type II region: \n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le x\\le 6yz+12}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of $R$ is given by the following triple integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & ={∭}_{R}\\text{d}V \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{6yz+12}\\,dx\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[x]_{x=0}^{x=6yz+12}\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(6yz+12)-0\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}6yz+12\\,dz\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[3y{z}^{2}+12z]_{z=0}^{z=1}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(3y(1)^{2}+12(1))-0\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}3y+12\\,dy \\\\  & ={[\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+12y]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}({2}^{2}-0)+12(2-0) \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
